docs {
  # POST /api/sales/done/ — Confirm sale (One Way, arrival only)

  Updates `Sale.passengers`/`details`, `Client.phone`, sets `paid=True`, creates `Transfer type="arrival"`. Requires `Authorization: Token {{token}}`. Source: `travels/views.py:137 SaleDoneView` + `serializers.py:112 SaleDoneSerializer`.

  Use when `service_type` is `One Way` (e.g., `1`) — departure fields omitted. `details` is optional.

  ## Status codes

  - `200 OK` — sale confirmed, arrival `Transfer` created
  - `400 Bad Request` — already paid (`"Sale already paid"`)
  - `401 Unauthorized` — invalid `stripe_code` or missing/invalid token

  ## Response (200)

  ```json
  {
    "status": "success",
    "message": "Sale confirmed successfully",
    "data": []
  }
  ```

  Creates 1 row `Transfer(type="arrival", date, hour, airline, flight_number, sale)` per `views.py:185`.

  ## Notes

  - `{{stripe_code}}` from `POST /api/sales/` `201`.
  - For Round Trip, see `post_confirm_round_trip.bru`.
}
